Move the New session screen's sandbox picker under the composer.

The picker of where the session runs, a sandbox or a connected host, was an
icon-only chip in the composer, left of the permission picker. It now leads
the workspace bar, before the repository (or the folder and branch on a
host), as a ComposerWorkspaceTrigger like the chips beside it: the sandbox's
name with the monitor-cloud icon, or a host's status dot, laptop icon and
name. Its menu is unchanged. Like the other chips it drops to its icon when
the bar is cramped, and it keeps the old chip's accessible name and title
("Host: Agent Sandbox, Offline"). The Codex theme draws the workspace bar
under the card; the other themes draw it as the tray above it. The
composer's environment menu in a session is unchanged.

The repository chip now starts further right, so its popover, lined up with
the chip's start and kept from flipping or sliding by 0006, was squeezed into
the room right of the chip on a phone. The popover now slides left on open
just far enough to keep its 24rem width, 8px off the screen's right edge.
Base: omnigent v0.15.0 (c8b9b85f822f), after 0022-start-without-message.patch.

